cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reference model or its derived application mappings, please cite this release and the underlying DIO/ODI publications."
title: "DIO/ODI Reference Model"
type: software
version: "0.9.0"
abstract: "Version 0.9.0 of the DIO/ODI Reference Model is a machine-readable SKOS-first reference layer for Digital Identity Optimization (DIO) and the Ontology of Digital Identity (ODI), with stable concept URIs, Turtle/RDF and JSON-LD serializations, provenance metadata, and explicitly separated non-normative application mappings. It carries forward Reference Vocabulary v0.2.2 with the disambiguated preferred compact prefix dio-odi, preserving the canonical namespace URI and all 40 concept URIs, together with the RAG, HEM, Commit-Boundary × Policy-as-Code, and Agentic ER mappings. This release updates the integrated Semantic Change Feed (SCF) to v0.1.1 with 45 documented events, a human-readable frontend, and JSON Schema v0.2.0. The SCF strengthens temporal and change provenance while remaining separate from the canonical vocabulary and derived mappings; it is not a Git commit log or a separate standalone publication. The Reference Model remains SKOS-first and makes no claim of implementation or empirical validation for its analytical mappings."
